ath: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]artifact_tranche_zero_and_generic_sidecar_roles.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-as[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page:[/dim]\n[#87AFFF]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-as/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Copy mode on every Artifacts sub-tab[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]copy-mode[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]copy-mode: admit `copy_tab_content` on non-PR Artifacts sub-tabs, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dispatch the second copy key on the active sub-tab before falling [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through to the tab id, add per-sub-tab copy key blocks and real copy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]menus for Commits, Plans, Chats, and Bugs, and make the COPY footer and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]its restore path sub-tab aware.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Marks on non-PR Artifacts sub-tabs[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]subtab-marks[dim] · [dim][/dim]after copy-mode[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]subtab-marks: route `toggle_mark`/`clear_marks` on the Artifacts tab [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the active sub-tab instead of the PR list, store marks per [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sub-tab keyed on the pane's existing stable entry target, render the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mark glyph, and let the sub-tab copy menus copy a marked set.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Anchored artifact-file path copy[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]path-copy[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]path-copy: stop emitting bare workspace-relative paths from the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]artifact-file modal's path copy, prefer the always-present stored path, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]anchor any source-path answer, and say in the toast which of the two was[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]copied.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Safe text-artifact fallback viewer[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]text-fallback[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]text-fallback: replace the bare `cat` fallback in the artifact text [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]viewer with a bounded, binary-detecting, control-sequence-neutralizing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reader and give the `bat` branch's argument-boundary hygiene to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fallback too.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Generic sidecar roles in the SDD store[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]store-roles[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]store-roles: replace the store record's fixed plans/research/beads [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fields with a role-keyed sidecar map, make `SddStore` resolve roots for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]any configured role, and stop requiring a sidecar literally named [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`research` before a sidecar-storage record can be written or considered [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]materialized.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Route hardcoded role tuples through the role registry[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]role-consumers[dim] · [dim][/dim]after store-roles[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]role-consumers: replace every remaining literal `(\"plans\", \"research\", [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]\"beads\")` tuple and `research`-named branch across repo inventory, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]linked-repo paths, `sase repo path`, doctor, commit finalization, SDD [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]path helpers, agent env, and the ACE file panel with the generic role [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]registry, and document the role model.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust core document corpora for plan discovery[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-corpora[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-corpora: teach the Rust plan reader to scan caller-supplied `(root,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]kind)` document corpora instead of only its hardcoded `plans`/`research`[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sub-directory pair, and expose that through `search_plans` and the PyO3 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`plan_search` binding without changing default behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plan search and CLI over document-sidecar roles[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]plan-search-roles[dim] · [dim][/dim]after store-roles, core-corpora[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan-search-roles: make the Python plan-search facade discover every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]configured document-sidecar root and pass them to the core as labeled [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]corpora, and make `sase plan search --kind` and its result styling [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]accept any discovered role rather than a fixed four-value choice list.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE Plans pane over every document sidecar[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ace-documents[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plan-search-